-- Hand-written below (ADR 0037): what the backup role app_backup may read. SELECT only, on
-- every table and sequence in public, now and later (no FOR ROLE: the role running the
-- migrations, app_owner, which creates every table), and drizzle's migration history, so a
-- restored database knows which migrations it already has. The policies above decide which
-- rows of a tenant table it sees: all of them.
GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA public TO app_backup;
--> statement-breakpoint
GRANT SELECT ON ALL SEQUENCES IN SCHEMA public TO app_backup;
--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES IN SCHEMA public GRANT SELECT ON TABLES TO app_backup;
--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES IN SCHEMA public GRANT SELECT ON SEQUENCES TO app_backup;
--> statement-breakpoint
GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA drizzle TO app_backup;
--> statement-breakpoint
GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA drizzle TO app_backup;
--> statement-breakpoint
GRANT SELECT ON ALL SEQUENCES IN SCHEMA drizzle TO app_backup;
